  {
    "type": "heading",
    "text": "3. UN Global Dialogue on AI Governance Opens in Geneva",
    "level": 3
  },
  {
    "type": "paragraph",
    "text": "CREDIBILITY: ★★★★★  ◆  CATEGORY: Global Governance  ◆  DATE: July 6, 2026"
  },
  {
    "type": "paragraph",
    "text": "Delegates from 169 countries convened in Geneva for the inaugural UN Global Dialogue on AI Governance, mandated by UN General Assembly Resolution A/RES/79/325. Co-chairs include Nobel laureate Maria Ressa and Turing Award winner Yoshua Bengio. The core question: can the world build shared AI governance without giving any single government unilateral power to deny access? Three competing philosophies are in play — US national security, EU regulatory, and Global South development-access."
