    "type": "heading",
    "text": "4. Alibaba Bans Claude Code Over Security Concerns",
    "level": 3
  },
  {
    "type": "paragraph",
    "text": "CREDIBILITY: ★★★★☆  ◆  CATEGORY: Geopolitics/Security  ◆  DATE: July 3–5, 2026"
  },
  {
    "type": "paragraph",
    "text": "Alibaba classified Anthropic's Claude Code as high-risk software and ordered employees to uninstall by July 10, citing alleged hidden detection mechanisms (China/timezone/proxy checks). Staff are directed to switch to Alibaba's own Qoder coding agent. This follows prior Anthropic accusations of large-scale distillation attacks by Alibaba-linked entities (~29M conversations)."
  },
  {
    "type": "paragraph",
    "text": "FACT CHECK: ⚠️ Reported by South China Morning Post and Reuters. The \"fingerprinting backdoor\" claim is attributed to reverse-engineering by third parties, not confirmed by Anthropic. Alibaba's ban is confirmed; the specific vulnerability claims should be treated as disputed."
  },
  {
    "type": "paragraph",
    "text": "SOURCES: South China Morning Post (scmp.com)  •  Reuters (reuters.com)"
